<title>CYPRUS: Hellenic first half profit rises.</title>
<headline>Hellenic first half profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hellenic Bank Ltd, the third largest banking group in Cyprus announced an operating profit of 4.08 million pounds in the first six months of 1996, a rise of 41.3 percent from 2.88 million in the first half of 1995.</p>
<p>Earlier this year Hellenic bought the Cyprus on-shore operations of Barclays Bank PLC.</p>
<p>-- Michele Kambas, Nicosia newsroom 357 2 365089</p>
